    "sourceUrl": "https://techspecs.ui.com/uisp/wired/es-24-500w",
    "note": "STILL NO PUBLISHED POE BUDGET, and the pass that added per-port direction did not invent one. The tech-spec page prints \"Power supply: AC/DC, internal, 500W\" and \"Max. power consumption: Includes PoE output: 500W / Excludes PoE output: 30W\" and no \"Total PoE available\" row - unlike its ES-24-250W sibling, whose page prints \"Total PoE available = 250W\". The quick-start guide (dl.ui.com/qsg/ES-24-250W_ES-24-500W/) prints the same 500 W without an allocation either. 500 W is the PSU rating and the whole-box ceiling including PoE, not watts reserved for powered devices, so budgetW stays null with budgetUnknown true. The per-port ceilings the page does print - 34.2 W PoE+ by PSE, 17 W 24V passive on the same jacks, not additive - are on the ports."
  },
  "notes": "Census from Ubiquiti's own two surfaces, read 2026-11-21. https://techspecs.ui.com/uisp/wired/es-24-500w (HTTP 200, 582,269 B, server-rendered table): Networking interface \"(24) 10/100/1000 Mbps RJ45 Ethernet ports / (2) 1 Gbps SFP ports\"; Management interface \"(1) RJ45 serial port, Ethernet In/Out-Band\"; Power supply \"AC/DC, internal, 500W\"; Max. power consumption \"Includes PoE output: 500W / Excludes PoE output: 30W\"; PoE interface \"PoE/PoE+ (Pins 1, 2+; 3, 6-) / 24V DC passive PoE (Pins 4, 5+; 7, 8-)\"; \"Max. PoE+ wattage per port by PSE 34.2W\"; \"Max. passive PoE wattage per port 17W\". The installation guide the same page links, https://dl.ui.com/qsg/ES-24-250W_ES-24-500W/ES-24-250W_ES-24-500W_EN.html (HTTP 200, 22,805 B), repeats the interface counts and the same 34.2 W / 17 W per-port ceilings, adds \"RJ45 PoE LED (Ports 1 - 24) ... Amber IEEE 802.3af/802.3at / Green 24V Passive\", and states \"The PoE settings for ports 1-24 are set to PoE+ auto by default, so 802.3af/at devices can be plugged in and automatically receive PoE\" - the shipped configuration, which is why the class word here is PoE+ and not passive. Before this pass the 24 copper ports carried no connector, no speedCaps and no poeOut, so engine/media.js derivePortHardware() handed every socket the 802.3af default of 15.4 W on a switch that supplies 34.2 W, and the serial console was absent (26 jacks modelled for 27 physical). Nothing here was inferred from the ES-24-250W: same enclosure, same guide, but each field above is a row on this model's own page."
